# Day 26

**18km / 4.5 hours**

Today was a short day, not totally by choice but by the whims of the tides. The issue is that the upcoming estuary is only reasonable to cross at low tide and the low tides currently are only in the early morning or evening and neither is very convenient for me. A shorter day wasn't so bad for me though, it doubled as a bit of a rest. 

It started fairly early and like many other days there wasn't much else to do other than prepare to leave. There was a light in the holiday park right next to the camping spot so there was light throughout the night.

![A sign in the city mentioning the Te Araroa!](./city-sign.jpg)

Getting going was in a park which was fairly pleasant and after dodging some runners doing a marathon. Then it was some city walking and road walking, pretty dull. Some of the following road walking was quite concerning as the road was narrow and windy that required ensuring getting out of the way of cars. 

![The view of the water from the track](./track-view.jpg)

Finally got to a nice track towards the campsite right before the estuary. The track was very pleasant with many nikau palm trees along the way. However reached this at noon which was far too early and meant I had lots of time to kill. Went for a short wade in the water and didn't get to the actually deep water despite going out quite far. Otherwise there wasn't much to do for the rest of the day other than rest.